  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: F_AuthRequired is the only fact directly forbidding a successful op with no caller (F_CallerIsTokenResolved is intentionally weakened to fire only when a caller exists). Removing it and forcing such an op makes the auth-required invariant fail.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: F_LeastPrivilege is the only fact tying Operation success to a matrix cell. Clearing it and forcing a successful Anonymous-role op produces an instance where (role -> kind) is not in PermMatrix.Allowed, which the LeastPrivilege predicate must reject.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionLogCompleteness  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionLogCompleteness.als
    rationale: F_DeletionLogCompleteness is the only fact requiring every successful delete to spawn a log entry. Clearing it and injecting a successful delete with no log directly contradicts the completeness predicate.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_DeletionRecorded, FR_018_DeletionLogged
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_DeletionRecorded: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionLogAttribution  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionLogAttribution.als
    rationale: F_DeletionLogAttribution is the only fact aligning a log entry's deleter/taskRef with the operation's caller/targetTask. Clearing it lets a delete op record a deleter different from its caller, which the AttributionCorrectness predicate explicitly rejects.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_018_DeletionLogged
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog.als
    rationale: F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog is the only fact enforcing a 1-to-1 mapping between log entries and successful delete operations. Removing it and forcing two distinct operations to share a single DeletionLogEntry constructs an instance the AppendOnly predicate must flag.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskEditRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskEditRule.als
    rationale: F_ClosedTaskEditRule is the only fact blocking a successful edit of a Done task that doesn't transition it out of Done. Clearing it and injecting such an edit (preStatus = newStatus = Done with outcome Success) violates the closed-task edit predicate directly.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskEdit
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskEdit: FAIL (expected)

